From acc4466c6b3d3a74087c14558d4f942749ce533e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Heimersheim <stefan.heimersheim@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 04:19:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] mptcp: account partially overlapping segments like the
 rest of the receive path

__mptcp_move_skb() has three ways of queueing an skb on the msk: in
sequence, out of order, and "partial packet" (map_seq < ack_seq < end_seq,
the already-acked prefix is skipped). The first two hand the skb to the
msk with mptcp_set_owner_r(), which charges the receive memory that
mptcp_rmem_schedule() reserved in msk->rmem_fwd_alloc and installs
mptcp_rfree() as destructor. The partial case uses the generic
skb_set_owner_r() instead: that charges sk_forward_alloc, which in this
kernel is the msk's *send* side pool, and frees through sock_rfree().
The reservation made in rmem_fwd_alloc for that skb is therefore never
consumed, the send-side pool is debited without a matching reservation,
and when the socket is destroyed the leftover is not a multiple of a page:

    WARNING: CPU: 0 PID: 2400 at net/ipv4/af_inet.c:156 inet_sock_destruct
    (WARN_ON_ONCE(sk_forward_alloc_get(sk)), msk destroyed from
     subflow_ulp_release() when its last subflow goes away)

With the default scheduler that path is only taken when a retransmitted
segment partially overlaps already received data, so the warning is
rare. With the redundant scheduler every byte arrives twice, and the
second subflow's segment boundaries are usually shifted against the
first one's, so partial overlaps happen thousands of times per
transfer and the warning fires on every run.

Use mptcp_set_owner_r() there as well. Current upstream has since moved
the msk receive accounting onto sk_forward_alloc altogether and uses
skb_set_owner_r() consistently, so this is specific to the rmem_fwd_alloc
scheme still present in 6.12.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/mptcp/protocol.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/protocol.c b/net/mptcp/protocol.c
index 6dd3fd847..221bea8c9 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/protocol.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/protocol.c
@@ -407,7 +407,7 @@ static bool __mptcp_move_skb(struct sock *sk, struct sk_buff *skb)
 	msk->bytes_received += copy_len;
 	WRITE_ONCE(msk->ack_seq, msk->ack_seq + copy_len);
 
-	skb_set_owner_r(skb, sk);
+	mptcp_set_owner_r(skb, sk);
 	__skb_queue_tail(&sk->sk_receive_queue, skb);
 	return true;
 }
